{
  "slug": "railscto",
  "name": "Railscto",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A complete Ruby on Rails toolkit for Claude Code: planning, idiomatic code, tests, linting, security scans, and git workflows — all enforced as non-negotiable QA gates.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **17 skills** and **3 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (17): `rails-cto` (Orchestrator skill for Ruby on Rails projects), `rails-cto-api` (How to build RESTful JSON APIs in a Rails 8 application following OpenAPI standards), `rails-cto-architect` (How to write comprehensive implementation plans for multi-step Rails features before any code is written), `rails-cto-commit` (Stage and commit all outstanding code changes with a clear, human-friendly commit message), `rails-cto-engineer` (This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with Ruby on Rails projects), `rails-cto-erb` (How to write clean, well-formatted ERB templates for this Rails 8 project), `rails-cto-minitest` (Write and maintain Minitest tests for a Rails 8 application using the Minitest::Spec DSL), `rails-cto-production-pr` (Create a production pull request merging staging into main using the gh CLI), and 9 more\n- **Hooks** (3): `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install railscto@claude-community` from `mattsears/rails-cto`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
